## Smell-Free Test

**`addThrowsOnNegativeCount`** (line 117) is well-written:

```java
IllegalArgumentException ex = assertThrows(
    IllegalArgumentException.class,
    () -> catalog.add("a", -1));
assertTrue(ex.getMessage().contains("non-negative"));
```

- Uses `assertThrows` (not manual `try/catch`)
- Asserts on the specific exception type
- Validates the message content
- Single focused behaviour

This is the pattern the other exception test should follow.

